The key property of the Delfos family is that all its questions are identically distributed random variables with the same expected value. Therefore, splitting them into two phases (each containing N questions) results in both phases having sample means that are unbiased estimators of the common expectation.

Thus, the final answer is:

\boxed{\text{All questions in the Delfos family are identically distributed with the same expectation}}

